      "worked_solution": "The opposite sides of a rectangle are congruent, so we have\n\n$$\nPL=MN=3\\,cm.\n$$\n\nFor the same reason, we also have\n\n$$\nNP=LM.\n$$\n\nNow, since the perimeter is $p=22\\,\\text{cm},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =LM+MN+NP+PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+2PL \\\\ 22 & =2NP+6 \\\\ 16 & =2NP \\\\ 8 & =NP\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $NP=8\\,\\text{cm}.$",
